# Work Done — Market Audit Platform (compiled from Claude session work)

This lists what was actually built/fixed in this working session, grouped by
feature area. This is based purely on the work done in this conversation — not
reconstructed from git history.

---

## 1. OneDrive "Upload to My OneDrive" — shared-folder fix

- Diagnosed why generated report zips weren't landing in a folder shared by
  another user (Shivam Pandey) — Microsoft Graph's `sharedWithMe` and
  `root/children` listings don't reliably surface a folder that was added to
  "My files" as a shortcut.
- Rebuilt folder discovery in `OneDrivePersonalService.php` to check both listing
  sources and prefer a shared match over an own-drive match.
- When that listing approach still proved unreliable, replaced it with **direct
  resolution via a configured sharing link** (Graph's `/shares/{id}/driveItem`),
  falling back to the original discovery logic only if that fails. Added
  `infiltration_shared_folder_url` to `config/services.php`.
- Diagnosed and resolved a separate **Azure AD admin-consent** problem that was
  blocking every non-admin user from connecting their OneDrive at all — the
  Delegated `Files.ReadWrite.All` permission had never actually been
  admin-consented on the app registration (only the unrelated Application-type
  permission had been).
- Confirmed via direct Graph API network capture and JWT scope inspection at
  each step, rather than guessing.

## 2. Verifier "pending" list bug fix

- Found why submitted auditor answers never showed up in the verifier's review
  queue: the pending-verification queries only matched `status = 0`, but a
  normal submission sets `status = 1`.
- Fixed in `VerifierController.php`: `activity_verification_data()`,
  `group_verification_data()`, and the approve/reject cleanup step inside
  `activity_answer_verify()`.

## 3. Digital signature capture

- Added an `activity_signatures` table/model earlier groundwork was extended:
  `uploadSignature()` now requires the activity to be fully closed before a
  signature can be attached.
- Added a `signature_allowed` flag to the mobile API responses (`getAllQuestion`,
  `getAllActivity`, the submit response in `saveAnswer`, and `closeActivity`) so
  the app knows when to prompt for a signature.
- Verifier review page (`verify.blade.php`) now displays the captured signature
  image.

## 4. "My Project Data" performance fix

- This admin page was computing full status/completion data for every row of a
  project (slow on ~3,000-row projects) before doing pagination client-side.
- Rewrote `userProjectMasterData()` in `TaskHandlerController.php` as a two-pass
  design: cheaply discover which rows match, paginate the row list first, then
  only run the expensive per-row computation for the current page's 10 rows.
- Replaced client-side DataTables pagination with a real search box and
  server-side pagination in `project_data.blade.php`.

## 5. New question type: Barcode / QR Code / RFID scanning

The largest piece of work, spanning the full pipeline end to end:

- **Template/admin setup** — added three new selectable question types to the
  Excel question template (`activityFormat.xlsx`) and the admin "Add Question"
  panel, repurposing the existing "Options" field so an admin can define the
  **expected header names** a scanned code should contain.
- **Import/save logic** — `ActivityController.php` and `QuestionController.php`
  parse those expected headers on both the Excel-upload and manual
  "Add Question" paths.
- **Live scanning UI** on the web auditor form
  (`activity_questions.blade.php`) — real camera-based barcode/QR scanning via
  the `html5-qrcode` library, and Web NFC-based RFID scanning (Chrome/Android
  only), with a plain manual-entry text field as the fallback everywhere else.
- Fixed a bug where a scanned value wasn't actually being saved — the page
  auto-saves each answer on the field losing focus (`blur`), but a
  JS-populated scan result never triggers a real blur event; fixed by
  explicitly triggering it after a successful scan.
- **Structured answer storage** — built a shared `ScanAnswerFormatter` service,
  used by both the mobile API (`TaskController::saveAnswer`) and the web form's
  auto-save endpoint (`TaskHandlerController::autoSaveAnswer`), so a scan is
  parsed identically regardless of which client submitted it. A scanned value is
  parsed as JSON or vCard where possible and stored as a structured record (raw
  value, parsed fields, which expected headers matched vs. which didn't),
  falling back to plain text for anything unparseable.
- **Report generation** — updated `ReportController.php` (both the main
  "Get Project Report" export and the separate "Distributor Report" export, and
  both their single-instance and repeat-instance sheet variants) so a scanned
  answer splits into one column/row per matched expected header, plus one more
  combined column/row (line-broken) for anything scanned that didn't match a
  configured header. Added wrap-text support to the custom `FastXlsxWriter`
  Excel writer to render those combined multi-line cells correctly.
- Extensively debugged real test data end-to-end during this work — traced
  issues back to: a QR code with a missing closing brace (genuinely invalid
  JSON, not a code bug), a server deployment mismatch, and stale/misconfigured
  question headers — confirming the final pipeline with a real scan producing
  the exact expected structured output.

## 6. Minor UI fix

- Made the "Select Activity" / "Select Group Activity" dropdowns on the
  activity-mapping page (`data_activity_mapping.blade.php`) searchable
  (Select2), matching the rest of that page — they were plain, unsearchable
  `<select>` elements.

